Both fixes are in, committed as 55604e4d (Part of #982). The full cargo test, clippy with -D warnings and fmt --check all pass.

What changed
• `yoyo config show` now exits 1 when a config file exists but can't be read. The stderr message ("Failed to read config file …") is the same as before. With no config file at all it still prints the defaults and exits 0. The REPL /config show prints exactly what it did before.
• `yoyo health zzz` now refuses the extra argument with exit 2, using the existing refuse_stray_arg helper like the other verbs. Plain yoyo health behaves as before: exit 1 outside a project.

Test: a new real-binary test in tests/integration.rs failed before the fix: config show exited 0 on an unreadable config. It passes now. It makes the config unreadable with a directory named .yoyo.toml instead of chmod 000, because root can't read a directory as a file either. It also points HOME and XDG_CONFIG_HOME at a temp dir, so a config on the test machine can't affect the "no config" check. It also checks that no config and plain health keep their old exit codes.

Other things in the commit
• src/dispatch_sub.rs went from 2521 to 2522 lines. That is over its entry in the file-size register in tests/module_size.rs, so I updated the entry and added a note saying why, as earlier changes did.
• Two doc sentences became false and are fixed: docs/src/usage/commands.md said config show always exits 0, and docs/src/troubleshooting/common-issues.md said "exit code still 0".

Issue: I commented on #982 with a before/after table and the commit sha. The comment says both items its latest comment (07:13Z) listed as still open are now fixed. One related case is still open and is a separate decision: a lint or health check that runs and fails still exits 0.
